186413186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413186 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "df76c1aa-2e4e-59a1-93d8-e361d723313c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413162 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413187 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f4d4aa4f-d888-5e28-9631-466adc355c5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186413168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186413165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413188 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f6ce2973-a27d-54ac-a874-d3afed02d1eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163804" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/62/6267809d1cc251384417967147434e9d44f4caf9e5fb0de1f10b0291952f75cf.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $A$ has mass $3\\,lb$ and is $6\\,yd$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1eab4807-9d88-5a37-9ff9-fc1404b92d43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413189 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $m$ be the mass of $B.$\nThe length of the rod is $8\\,yd$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,yd.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is\n\n$$\n8-6=2\\,yd,\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f3/f3efa18d3ae4e9a7f23f805dd314b9d04f50bb03ec3ead20a82a8e4c586e96a7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot 6=-18\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $m\\cdot 2=2m\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-18+2m & =0 \\\\ 2m & =18 \\\\ m & =9\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/17/17b621de27c4ad429c44ce1a91cd254c885ee83e7d97b03410cae64c3fc52284.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26263261-ed01-57e5-8398-ad944dae02a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413190 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1, & \\,{m}_{3} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+1+6 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 3+6\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =3+3+24 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{30}{10}=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/a4/a4f6cf6f453399ec8b823a447bfb93b1b33668004c22c15dc5b42c413f6226bb.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $9\\,kg$ and $3\\,kg$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $4\\,m$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ec15158-435a-5888-95f3-44340c0036cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413191 #edb/ref 1074 "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/b3/b3650c27d30a72df4d92b4eed8f4cfff71d598b1821d0541632b38722d854210.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-9\\cdot {d}_{1}=-9{d}_{1}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $3\\cdot {d}_{2}=3{d}_{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n3{d}_{2}-9{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{2},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{1}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $4\\,m,$ we have\n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{d}_{1}=4-{d}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{d}_{2}-9(4-{d}_{2}) & =0 \\\\ 3{d}_{2}-36+9{d}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 12{d}_{2} & =36 \\\\ {d}_{2} & =3\\,m.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413175 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163832" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0f/0fcb0a0dd58506c39c038cb55b702ae965251dab55f5db477b0f0f6d275240f9.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $3\\,lb$ and $5\\,lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $8\\,yd$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. Find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47a5c5c7-d82d-5d72-883d-d0468b52660c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413192 #edb/ref 1074 "Let ${d}_{1}$ and ${d}_{2}$ be the distances between the fulcrum and $A$ and $B$, respectively, as shown below.\n\n![](images/80/800da868d66524a7970a2ee421af15f64ca0b8019b4c0572209c183245e4cce7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-3\\cdot {d}_{1}=-3{d}_{1}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $5\\cdot {d}_{2}=5{d}_{2}\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe principle of moments tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero. \n\nSo, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n5{d}_{2}-3{d}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe need to find ${d}_{1},$ so we eliminate ${d}_{2}.$\nUsing the fact that the rod has length $8\\,yd,$ we have \n\n$$\n{d}_{1}+{d}_{2}=8\\,⟹\\,{d}_{2}=8-{d}_{1}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(8-{d}_{1})-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 40-5{d}_{1}-3{d}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 8{d}_{1} & =40 \\\\ {d}_{1} & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/8f/8fa845de716b1043248c3fb7d185e241d3d89688b185901b4b8275a6c89368f3.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66bc40ec-8b7f-5a7f-a822-c2240ee2d9f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413193 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =3, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3+1.5\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-6+6+6 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $6\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f4/f4950acfb535c32e4f7e275bcd17b72717c717c5a4ed17834d6a9c5561cc433e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "71003ac4-a6c7-5375-9693-7a03dcbed8fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413194 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=1,\\,{m}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=2,\\,{y}_{2}=0,\\,{y}_{3}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+1+3 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8+0+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{20}{8}=\\frac{5}{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/4b/4bd2a8d5a2bdb2400646031be209e9bdf8ffaf985c9f5f9672ec1709a8e9947f.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $5\\,lb$ and $6lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is $6\\,ft,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77273bb6-e09c-5d72-b951-ab16051ede43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413195 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $B,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/cb/cbde3ab8e8ebbeae51a4840bf69d729f1bdbe310ac798d378d59290cd9d4f5c7.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-5\\cdot 6=-30\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $6\\cdot d=6d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6d-30 & =0 \\\\ 6d & =30 \\\\ d & =5\\,ft.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163266" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ec/ec5be4034607896656ff6613f05843529f6673783fdb30fdd4eb355c3acf6573.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ff6628f-789d-5102-a51c-36a2bdf1a544" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413196 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =4, & \\,{m}_{2} & =7, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+7+1 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+7\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =12+28+8 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{48}{12}=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/86/8628c638fd2820222f494bb2a06bc685964cf9da249fa64e953040ac623faeb7.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4435932-14e7-5d5c-ae2a-cc6b7883581b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413197 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=3,\\,{m}_{3}=5.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=2,\\,{y}_{2}=-1,\\,{y}_{3}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =4+3+5 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =8-3+15 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{20}{12}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/21/216250fd3d35779c87c90a0eacc6c05c4084e1eb4d602f65051372b0ada2e45f.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{y}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b1025740-1de0-548c-b755-7aea427a0e9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413198 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=4,\\,{m}_{2}=2,\\,{m}_{3}=2,\\,{m}_{4}=6.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}=1,\\,{y}_{2}=4,\\,{y}_{3}=1,\\,{y}_{4}=3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =4+2+2+6 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3}+{m}_{4}{y}_{4} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4+8+2+18 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}=\\frac{32}{14}=\\frac{16}{7}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163192" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=1.5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{3}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{4}=5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-3\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=-2\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{3}=4\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{4}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9628c5b-7fa0-5045-9ac2-ad280b61b082" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413199 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =1.5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4, & \\,{x}_{4} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+1.5\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4+5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-9-3+12+30 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $30\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/88/88a0ceeb1f98bd909ebc6eda2c5232075b6f93d4a158ae1ed1cb4943ab08424c.png)\n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ of mass $12\\,lb$ and $15lb$, respectively, are connected by a rigid, massless rod that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,yd,$ find the distance between the fulcrum and $A.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c47fff30-dc4f-5860-a5ab-d77dfee6da24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413200 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $d$ be the distance between the fulcrum and $A,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/ee/eeaf2a4fbefd3066d28fab6b52cbea58f5adac5cd35887ad012691c9847f5caa.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-12\\cdot d=-12d\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $15\\cdot 4=60\\,\\text{lb}\\cdot \\text{yd}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to perfectly balance, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}60-12d & =0 \\\\ 12d & =60 \\\\ d & =5\\,yd.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=3\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=6\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=2,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3}=5,$ respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c57b76e6-1edf-5c3c-98a4-e16cf256a5f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413201 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =5, & \\,{m}_{3} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2, & \\,{x}_{2} & =4, & \\,{x}_{3} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+6 \\\\  & =14\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 4+6\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =6+20+30 \\\\  & =56\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{56}{14}=4.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163263" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e0/e025510c351042df35e2c077a4179e808e5fac47d9dad3530e2aaa7346818055.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cd5d39c2-8301-5260-adfd-2e9f69bcfb7d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413202 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{―}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =3, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =5, & \\,{m}_{4} & =6, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3, & \\,{x}_{2} & =-1.5, & \\,{x}_{3} & =2, & \\,{x}_{4} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =3+2+5+6 \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot (-1.5)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-9-3+10+18 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{16}{16}=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the collection of point masses ${m}_{1}=5\\,\\text{kg},$ ${m}_{2}=4\\,\\text{kg},$ and ${m}_{3}=2.5\\,\\text{kg}$ located at ${x}_{1}=-1\\,\\text{m},$ ${x}_{2}=1\\,\\text{m},$ and ${x}_{3}=6\\,\\text{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3c48087-507b-57b2-8663-35cf3ca6e4b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413203 #edb/ref 1074 "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n{M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =5, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =2.5, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+2.5\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-5+4+15 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $14\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\text{m}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186413176 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163267" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7e/7ef79655f2689ab5987631a89ccb8d91c0ed6f67375750f6c0720224f92dddd6.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$ and $y$ axes are measured in meters. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overset{―}{x}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7aab632-bc8c-5d87-8d6b-6366b876ba3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413204 #edb/ref 1074 "The center of mass of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},…,{m}_{n}$ located at $({x}_{1}{y}_{1}),({x}_{2},{y}_{2}),…,({x}_{n},{y}_{n})$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{m}),\n$$\n\n \nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{x}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- ${M}_{y}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $y$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\n{m}_{1}=3,\\,{m}_{2}=6,\\,{m}_{3}=4,\\,{m}_{4}=2.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $x$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=-4,\\,{x}_{2}=-1,\\,{x}_{3}=3,\\,{x}_{4}=4.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3}+{m}_{4} \\\\  & =3+6+4+2 \\\\  & =15\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-4)+6\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-12-6+12+8 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{m}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
